                                                <h2 class="text-size-large font-weight-medium text-gray-nine-hundred title-font margin-bottom-two">Design That Starts With Listening</h2>
                                                <p class="leading-relaxed margin-bottom-six">
                                                      A useful design direction begins with understanding what matters to the people who use the space. Conversations about routines, preferences, existing furniture and the atmosphere a client wants can help define the brief before visual decisions are made. This avoids treating a home as a blank canvas with a predetermined look. Instead, ideas can respond to the room, its occupants and its practical requirements. The result is a more considered
                                                      process in which style choices have a clear relationship to how the home is lived in.
                                                </p>
