                                                <h2 class="text-size-large font-weight-medium text-gray-nine-hundred title-font margin-bottom-two">A Clearer View of Layout</h2>
                                                <p class="leading-relaxed margin-bottom-six">
                                                      The arrangement of a room affects how it feels and functions, from circulation between areas to the placement of furniture and everyday objects. Taking time to consider scale, movement and the purpose of each zone can make design decisions easier to evaluate. Layout discussions can also help identify what should remain, what might be repositioned and where a room could benefit from a different balance. Rather than assuming that more furniture
                                                      or decoration is the answer, the focus is on making the available space feel coherent and comfortable.
                                                </p>
