                                                <h2 class="text-size-large font-weight-medium text-gray-nine-hundred title-font margin-bottom-two">Materials and Colours With Purpose</h2>
                                                <p class="leading-relaxed margin-bottom-six">
                                                      Finishes, fabrics and colours contribute to the character of an interior, but they also need to make sense together and suit the way a space is used. A considered palette can connect rooms, highlight architectural features or create a calmer atmosphere, while material choices can add texture and visual interest. Exploring these elements as part of an overall direction helps prevent isolated decisions from competing with one another. The aim
                                                      is not to follow a passing trend, but to make choices that feel appropriate to the home and its owners.
                                                </p>
