                                                <p class="leading-relaxed margin-bottom-six">
                                                      A home often feels most distinctive when its design makes room for the objects, memories and preferences that are meaningful to its occupants. Personal details do not have to overwhelm a room; they can be considered alongside lighting, artwork, furnishings and useful storage. Taking a measured approach helps create a balance between a polished overall look and the qualities that make a space feel lived in. The design conversation can
